  'tbl.howTitle': 'How to read this table',
  'tbl.how1': 'The Status column comes from the alert thresholds (Settings → Alert thresholds): the Critical and High day limits are configurable; Expired means days remaining is negative; Error means the certificate could not be read.',
  'tbl.how2': 'Trust summarises three independent checks: chain integrity, CA trust and revocation (OCSP/CRL). A certificate the browser would reject shows red here even when its expiry is far away.',
  'tbl.how3': 'The bar under Days left shows how much of the lifetime has been used: 40 days left on a 90-day certificate means "renew now"; on a 397-day one it is early.',
  'tbl.how4': 'A "stale" mark on Last check means the row has not been refreshed for more than twice the domain\'s check interval — run Check now.',
  'tbl.how5': 'Filters are written to the address bar: copy the link to share a view, or save one you use often as a preset. CSV downloads every page with the same filters.',
  'tbl.help.status': 'Server verdict: Expired (days left < 0) · Critical (≤ critical threshold) · High (≤ high threshold) · Warning (inside the warning window) · Valid · Error (unreadable). Thresholds are managed under Settings → Alert thresholds; cards and this table read the same verdict.',
