  'scripted.subtitle': 'Runs user-defined k6 scripts periodically to synthetically monitor multi-step flows (OIDC/Keycloak login, API chains) end to end.',
  'scripted.how1': 'The k6 binary is run on the monitoring server (single pod) as a short-lived subprocess (not embedded); path site.monitor.scripted.k6-bin. Presence/version are probed at startup and every 5 min; if k6 is missing this type is disabled. Egress: when a corporate proxy is configured k6 uses it (the monitor’s “Proxy” setting); under Automatic, targets matching NO_PROXY as a SUFFIX go DIRECT — “Always via proxy” ignores that list; the corporate CA bundle is passed to k6 as well.',
  'scripted.how2': 'Execution: k6 run --vus 1 --iterations 1 (single iteration); a --blacklist-ip is added for every SSRF blacklist CIDR (internal/loopback/metadata blocked). Timeout defaults to 60s (floor 5, ceiling 180); on overrun SIGTERM→SIGKILL. Concurrency is bounded by a pool (default 2).',
  'scripted.how3': 'Environment variables/secrets are passed only into the subprocess environment (read in-script via __ENV); secret values are decrypted but masked out of captured output; hardcoded secrets are scanned and warned at save time.',
  'scripted.how4': 'Result: timeout ⇒ TIMEOUT; exit code ≠0 and ≠99 ⇒ ERROR; exit 99 or any failed k6 check ⇒ FAIL; NO_CHECKS if no check ran; otherwise PASS. If the check could NOT be executed at all (k6 pool saturated / k6 missing) the result is SKIPPED: nothing is recorded and no alert is raised — infrastructure saturation is not an outage. Every run stores the request phase breakdown (DNS → TCP → TLS → send → wait → receive) and bytes transferred; the “Where did it get stuck?” panel shows it. When “Slow-run alert” is enabled on the monitor, runs that PASS but exceed the threshold raise a separate SCRIPTED_SLOW alert (same 3× confirm and recovery chain). The “Connection Diagnostics” tab probes the same target with proxy/CA combinations.',
  'scripted.how5': 'JavaScript level: k6 compiles the script with an embedded transpiler — the syntax is frozen at ES2017 (?. , ?? and {...object} DO NOT COMPILE), while library functions are modern. Compilation is attempted at save time via k6 archive; a definite syntax error is rejected with its line/column. See the Guide for details and an example.',
  'scripted.refresh': 'Refresh', 'scripted.addMonitor': 'New Monitor',
  'scripted.k6Disabled': 'Synthetic Monitoring disabled — k6 not found in this environment. The k6 binary must be added to the Docker image.',
  'scripted.k6VersionTitle': 'Your scripts run against this environment\'s k6 version',
  'scripted.k6LegacySyntax': 'The engine in this version CANNOT parse `?.`, `??` or `{...object}` (bundled Babel 6) — use classic `&&` / `||` and `Object.assign`. Array spread `[...array]` works.',
  'scripted.k6ModernSyntax': 'Modern JavaScript syntax (`?.`, `??`, object spread) is supported.',
