  'mhow.title': 'How and where are these checks done?',
  'guideForm.btn': 'How to fill',
  'guideForm.title': 'How to fill the new monitor form',
  'dom.howTitle': 'How and where are these checks done?',
  'dom.how1': 'RDAP (primary): the TLD\'s official RDAP server is found via the IANA bootstrap (through the corporate proxy); on miss it falls back to rdap.org.',
  'dom.how2': 'WHOIS (RDAP-less TLDs such as .tr): expiry is obtained via HTTPS web-whois — it runs over 443, so it passes the corporate proxy (on by default). Sources are tried in order, first parseable answer wins: ① isimtescil.net (plain GET, ...?domainname=<domain>) → ② TRABIS official web (trabis.gov.tr; CSRF token + session form POST) → ③ raw port-43 WHOIS (whois.trabis.gov.tr; last resort — usually skipped since the corporate firewall blocks port 43). All three return the exact same TRABIS record; only the transport differs. WHICH source answered is shown on the "Diagnose" card. For classic gTLDs expiry comes from RDAP; if neither RDAP nor whois returns data the status becomes UNKNOWN.',
  'dom.how3': 'Registrable domain: a URL/subdomain is reduced to eTLD+1 via the Public Suffix List (www.x.com.tr → x.com.tr); IDN is converted to punycode.',
  'dom.how4': 'Collected data: expiry/creation dates, registrar, EPP status codes (redemptionPeriod/hold → critical) and nameservers.',
  'dom.how5': 'DNS cross-check: whether the domain\'s NS records resolve. Checks run once per day (with jitter); history is retained.',
  'dom.how6': 'Change & UNKNOWN: a registrar/NS/status change raises a separate alarm (possible hijack); if no data can be obtained, UNKNOWN is also an alarm — "no data ≠ no problem".',
  'dom.how7': 'Troubleshooting: use "Diagnose" on a domain to inspect the PSL → RDAP (bootstrap/registry/rdap.org) → .tr web-whois (isimtescil/TRABIS/:43) chain step by step; you see each step\'s latency, error and the source that answered. You can also enter a full URL (https://www.domain.com.tr/ → domain.com.tr). Set the RDAP timeout per monitor, and capture the proxy SSL-inspection root CA from Settings → Domain Diagnostics if needed.',
  'dom.on': 'Yes', 'dom.off': 'No',
  'dom.check': 'Check now', 'dom.edit': 'Edit',
