  'http.pageTitle':   'HTTP / Website Monitoring',
  'http.subtitle':    'Monitor the availability of websites, API endpoints and HTTP services.',
  'http.how1': 'A direct HTTP(S) request is made from the monitoring server (single pod) — GET/HEAD/POST, 10s connect timeout. Only the status code and response time are measured (the body is discarded). The egress path follows the form\'s “Corporate proxy” setting: Same as inventory (default) = via the proxy when the domain\'s certificate-inventory record has “Check via proxy = Yes”, otherwise straight from the pod; Always via proxy / Direct pin it. Same proxy and same NO_PROXY rule as certificate checks; the Proxy / Direct badge on the card shows the path actually taken.',
  'http.how2': 'Healthy = status code matches the expected pattern (e.g. 200, 2xx, 200-399; blank defaults to 200–399). Whether redirects are followed is controlled by the "follow redirects" toggle.',
  'http.how3': 'SSL-verify toggle: off measures reachability only (internal-CA/self-signed certs are fine); on validates the certificate against the JVM/corporate-CA bundle/auto-pinned host CA — on a PKIX trust failure (if auto-pin is on) the server CA is pinned and retried once. TLS errors count as unreachable.',
  'http.how4': 'Before the request an SSRF guard blocks cloud-metadata/loopback/link-local targets. For multi-A hosts the first reachable IP is tried, with SNI = domain.',
