  'help.set.site.monitor.login.ldap-enabled':
    'What it does: Switches password sign-in for LDAP (Active Directory) accounts on or off; while off, those accounts can only sign in with a code.\nBenefit: Password sign-in can be stopped with one click during an LDAP problem or by policy; directory sync is not affected.\nRecommended: true (the default). Enable at least one code method before switching it off; local accounts and the installation administrator can always sign in.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.push.enabled':
    'What it does: Lets users sign in with a one-time 6-digit code delivered by push notification.\nBenefit: During an LDAP problem or a forgotten password, users can sign in with the code on their mobile device.\nRecommended: false (the default). Without a configured push gateway it stays hidden on the sign-in page even when switched on.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.email.enabled':
    'What it does: Lets users sign in with a one-time 6-digit code sent to the email address on their account.\nBenefit: A second code sign-in route for people who do not use push.\nRecommended: false (the default). Email delivery must be faster than the code validity period.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.push.ttl-seconds':
    'What it does: How many seconds a code sent by push stays valid.\nBenefit: A short lifetime reduces the chance of a stolen code being used.\nRecommended: 45 seconds (the default). Range 30–300.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.email.ttl-seconds':
    'What it does: How many seconds a code sent by email stays valid.\nBenefit: Leaves room for email delays while still limiting the lifetime of the code.\nRecommended: 45 seconds (the default), or 90–120 if your mail server is slow. Range 30–300.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.max-attempts':
    'What it does: How many incorrect attempts are allowed for a single code; once exceeded, the code is locked.\nBenefit: Prevents the code from being guessed.\nRecommended: 3 (the default). Range 1–10.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.resend-cooldown-seconds':
    'What it does: How long to wait before a new code can be sent for the same user and channel.\nBenefit: Stops a user from being flooded with notifications or emails.\nRecommended: 30 seconds (the default). Range 10–300.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.max-requests-per-user':
    'What it does: The maximum number of codes sent to one user in 15 minutes; any more are silently not sent.\nBenefit: Limits someone else requesting codes in your name; the response stays the same, so account existence does not leak.\nRecommended: 5 (the default). Range 1–20.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.max-requests-per-ip':
    'What it does: The maximum number of codes that can be requested from one IP address in 15 minutes; any more are refused.\nBenefit: Slows down bulk attempts and username scanning from a single source.\nRecommended: 20 (the default), or 50–100 if your users sit behind a shared NAT. Range 1–500.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.max-failed-verifications':
    'What it does: The total number of incorrect codes allowed for one user in 15 minutes; once exceeded, code sign-in is suspended for that user.\nBenefit: Makes guessing a code practically impossible; password sign-in and the account lock are not affected.\nRecommended: 5 (the default). Range 1–20.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.allow-global-admins':
    'What it does: Allows global administrators to sign in with a code as well.\nBenefit: Administrators can sign in during an LDAP problem; while off, the most privileged accounts stay protected by password only.\nRecommended: false (the default). The installation administrator can always sign in with a password.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.push.require-phone':
    "What it does: A push code request also asks for the registered mobile number next to the username; the code is sent only if both belong to the same account.\nBenefit: Someone who only knows a username cannot send codes to another person's phone; a mismatching number is never revealed on screen.\nRecommended: true (the default). When off, a code is requested with the username only.",
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.email.require-email':
    "What it does: An email code request also asks for the registered email address next to the username; the code is sent only if both belong to the same account.\nBenefit: Someone who only knows a username cannot send codes to another person's mailbox; a mismatching address is never revealed on screen.\nRecommended: true (the default). When off, a code is requested with the username only.",
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.max-contact-mismatches':
    'What it does: The number of mismatching phone / email attempts accepted for one username in 15 minutes; once exceeded, code requests for that user are silently suppressed.\nBenefit: Prevents finding the registered number or address by trial and error; password sign-in and the account lock are not affected.\nRecommended: 5 (the default). Range 1–20.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.retention-days':
    'What it does: How many days code sign-in requests (code hash, status, IP) are kept; older rows are removed by the nightly clean-up.\nBenefit: Request rows are only useful for a few minutes; the permanent trail is in the audit log anyway.\nRecommended: 30 days (the default).',
  // ── Sign-in methods: push message editor (2026-10-03) ──
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.push.title-tr':
    'What it does: The Turkish title of the code sign-in push notification; it goes to people who use the sign-in page in Turkish.\nBenefit: The notification is recognised at once on the lock screen under the name people are used to.\nRecommended: blank (default "SiteMonitor giriş kodu"). At most 60 characters; placeholders cannot be used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.push.title-en':
    'What it does: The English title of the code sign-in push notification; it goes to people who use the sign-in page in English.\nBenefit: The notification is recognised at once on the lock screen under the name people are used to.\nRecommended: blank (default "SiteMonitor sign-in code"). At most 60 characters; placeholders cannot be used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.push.message-tr':
    'What it does: The Turkish text of the code sign-in push notification; {kod} is filled with the 6-digit code, {sure} with the validity and {saat} with the time of the request.\nBenefit: Users are reached in the organisation\'s own words and warnings; the text cannot exceed the push message limit, so the code is never cut off.\nRecommended: blank (the default text). {kod} must appear exactly once.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.login.otp.push.message-en':
    'What it does: The English text of the code sign-in push notification; {kod} is filled with the 6-digit code, {sure} with the validity and {saat} with the time of the request.\nBenefit: Users are reached in the organisation\'s own words and warnings; the text cannot exceed the push message limit, so the code is never cut off.\nRecommended: blank (the default text). {kod} must appear exactly once.',
  'audit.ev.LOGIN_METHODS_PUSH_TEST': 'Sign-in code push text tested',
