  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.overflow-summary-enabled':
    'What it does: Combines pushes held back by the hourly limit into ONE summary push per person ("14 notifications were held back (3 critical, 11 warning). Latest: …"); no links, in the person\'s language.\nBenefit: People learn they missed something with a single notification instead of silence, and their phone is not flooded.\nRecommended: true (default). When off, held-back pushes only stay in the delivery log as RATE_LIMITED.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.overflow-summary-minutes':
    'What it does: How long after the first unsummarised overflow the summary goes out, and the shortest gap between two summaries for one person (minutes).\nBenefit: During a wide outage a person gets one summary per interval, not one every minute.\nRecommended: 15 (default); allowed range 5-120. 10 for on-call teams, 30 for wide distribution.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.critical-bypass-cap':
    'What it does: When on, CRITICAL alert pushes are never held back by the hourly limit (they still count towards it).\nBenefit: During a wide outage a critical alert is not lost behind the flood of warnings before it.\nRecommended: false (default, today\'s behaviour). Set true if a critical alert must always reach the phone.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.escalation.step-push-enabled':
    'What it does: When a timed escalation step is sent and the contact matches exactly ONE active user (explicit link or a unique e-mail), the step is also pushed.\nBenefit: An unacknowledged alert also reaches the phone of an escalation contact who is not reading e-mail right then.\nRecommended: true (default). It has no effect while no delayed escalation contact exists.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.title.en':
    'What it does: The title of pushes sent to people whose push language is English.\nBenefit: English-speaking people see the title in their language too.\nRecommended: Empty (the Turkish title is used) or a short English name; a product name usually stays untranslated.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.down.en':
    'What it does: English template of the OUTAGE (down) push; the placeholders are the same as in the Turkish template (e.g. {seviye}, {ad}, {neden}).\nBenefit: People whose push language is English read the alert in their language.\nRecommended: One line, under 200 characters. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.slow.en':
    'What it does: English template of the THRESHOLD BREACH (slow) push; the placeholders are the same as in the Turkish template (e.g. {metrik}, {deger}, {esik}).\nBenefit: People whose push language is English read the alert in their language.\nRecommended: One line, under 200 characters. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.expiry.en':
    'What it does: English template of the EXPIRY push; the placeholders are the same as in the Turkish template (e.g. {ne}, {gun}, {tarih}).\nBenefit: People whose push language is English read the alert in their language.\nRecommended: One line, under 200 characters. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.changed.en':
    'What it does: English template of the CHANGE (changed) push; the placeholders are the same as in the Turkish template (e.g. {degisen}, {baslangic}).\nBenefit: People whose push language is English read the alert in their language.\nRecommended: One line, under 200 characters. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.cert.en':
    'What it does: English template of the CERTIFICATE DEFECT (cert) push; the placeholders are the same as in the Turkish template (e.g. {ip}, {cn}, {neden}).\nBenefit: People whose push language is English read the alert in their language.\nRecommended: One line, under 200 characters. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.degraded.en':
    'What it does: English template of the DEGRADED (not an outage) push; the placeholders are the same as in the Turkish template (e.g. {neden}, {baslangic}).\nBenefit: People whose push language is English read the alert in their language.\nRecommended: One line, under 200 characters. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.resolved.en':
    'What it does: English template of the RESOLVED push; the placeholders are the same as in the Turkish template (e.g. {sure}, {baslangic}, {bitis}).\nBenefit: People whose push language is English read that the alert closed, in their language.\nRecommended: One line, under 200 characters. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',
  'help.set.site.monitor.userpush.template.test.en':
    'What it does: English template of the administrator test send (placeholder {saat}).\nBenefit: A real send confirms how the English template looks on the phone.\nRecommended: A short test sentence. If left empty, the built-in English default is used.',

