  'mcert.guide.hint': 'Formats, passwords, what not to upload and privacy',
  'mcert.guide.intro': 'Site Monitor takes no part in requesting, signing or installing certificates; it only tracks a certificate’s expiry and health. A file containing the certificate itself (its public chain) is all it needs.',
  'mcert.guide.whenTitle': 'When to upload',
  'mcert.guide.step1': 'A CSR is requested through an internal ticket; a zip containing the CSR arrives by email.',
  'mcert.guide.step2': 'The CSR is sent to the external certificate authority (CA).',
  'mcert.guide.step3': 'The CA sends back the signed certificate (for example xxxx.pem) — you can upload this file.',
  'mcert.guide.step4': 'The chain is completed and a PFX or JKS is produced — uploading this complete-chain file is better.',
  'mcert.guide.step5': 'The keystore / truststore JKS is installed on OpenShift. You can also track the CA certificates in the truststore one by one.',
